     not have such rules, and the check incorrectly disallows valid requirement
     strings from being parsed.
 
+``Requirement.__replace__()`` accepts the keyword arguments ``name``, ``url``,
+``extras`` (a set of strings), ``specifier`` (a ``SpecifierSet``), and ``marker``
+(a ``Marker`` or ``None``). Omitted fields are retained. The result is parsed
+and normalized, and invalid or ambiguous values raise ``InvalidRequirement``.
+Unknown keywords raise ``TypeError``. Specifier prerelease overrides are
+preserved, and mutable fields are independent of the original and supplied
+values. Subclasses are constructed through their own initializer.
+
